claim.claim-text:
identifying an HTTP page-start transaction from traffic data in a communication network;
detecting if the HTTP page-start transaction contains a start of a web page;
assigning a page classification to the HTTP page-start transaction based on contents of one or more packets in the HTTP page-start transaction and at least one classification override rule;
identifying a subsequent HTTP transaction from the traffic data;
determining whether the subsequent HTTP transaction is part of the web page;
automatically assigning the page classification to the subsequent HTTP transaction, without application of any classification override rules, if the subsequent HTTP transaction is part of the web page; and
repeating the identifying a subsequent HTTP transaction, determining, and automatically assigning until a page end criteria is reached.
